{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"106531","commit":"14527caf012faf2f217b26520dcf1874e228b066","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The introduction of the `ProfileService` and its integration with API key retrieval actions (`TransportGetApiKeyAction` and `TransportQueryApiKeyAction`) is a significant change. The code now includes functionality to resolve profile UIDs for API keys, which involves additional steps in both action classes. This change enhances the capability to fetch more detailed information about API keys, including their associated profiles.\nThe `ApiKeyService` and its methods (`getApiKeys` and `queryApiKeys`) have been updated to support the new functionality. The `TransportGetApiKeyAction` and `TransportQueryApiKeyAction` now call these methods with an additional listener that processes the API key information to resolve profile UIDs if requested. This ensures that the actions return the correct response format, including the owner\u0027s profile UID when applicable.\nThe `ProfileService` class has been updated to include a method `resolveProfileUidsForApiKeys`, which takes a collection of API keys and returns their corresponding profile UIDs. This method uses the existing `searchProfilesForSubjects` method to fetch the profiles for the subjects associated with the API keys. The `getApiKeyCreatorSubject` method is used to create a `Subject` object from an `ApiKey` instance, which is then used to search for the profile.\nThe `ApiKey` class has been updated to include methods for retrieving the realm type and identifier. These methods are used in the `ProfileService` to determine the realm configuration of the API key creator.\nThe `Security` class has been updated to create a `ProfileService` instance with the realms object instead of a domain configuration lookup function. This change aligns with the new requirements for resolving profile UIDs based on realm information.\nThe `QueryApiKeyRequest` class has been updated to include a new boolean field for fetching the profile UID. This change ensures that the request can specify whether it wants to retrieve the owner\u0027s profile UID along with the API key information.\nThe `ApiKeyServiceTests` class has been updated to include tests for the new functionality. These tests ensure that the API key retrieval actions correctly handle requests with and without the profile UID flag.\nThe `ApiKeyOwnerProfileIntegTests` class has been added to test the integration of API keys with profiles. These tests cover scenarios where API keys are created and managed by users with different roles and realms, ensuring that the profile information is correctly associated with the API keys.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/security/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/authc/ApiKeyIntegTests.java-x-pack/plugin/security/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/authc/ApiKeyIntegTests.java--173590:174897","promptId":"#9DBQ6","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/security/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/authc/ApiKeyIntegTests.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/security/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/authc/ApiKeyIntegTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":173590,"endPos":174897,"startLine":3408,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":3434,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1308}]},{"id":"-x-pack/plugin/security/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/profile/ApiKeyOwnerProfileIntegTests.java--1784:19723","promptId":"#0N5RV","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/security/src/internalClusterTest/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/profile/ApiKeyOwnerProfileIntegTests.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1784,"endPos":19723,"startLine":39,"startLineOffset":0,"endLine":378,"endLineOffset":1,"length":17940}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/security/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/security/profile/ProfileService.java-x-pack/plugin/security/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/secu